# Spark Workflow Rules

## Medallion-First
Define Bronze/Silver/Gold layers before writing transforms. Each layer has an explicit schema documented in the job config before any code is written. Layer boundaries are enforced — no skipping from Bronze directly to Gold.

## Local-First Development
Develop and test with small datasets locally using `SparkSession` with `master("local[2]")`. No cluster is required for unit tests. All transform logic must be verifiable on a laptop before submission to a cluster.

## chispa Test Loop
Write a failing chispa test → implement the transform → make it green. Do not submit to a cluster to verify transform logic — that is what unit tests are for. If you cannot test it with chispa, refactor the transform until you can.

## CI Gate
`ruff check` → `mypy` → `pytest` → integration test on sample data. All steps must pass before a PR can be merged. No exceptions. A red CI is a blocker, not a warning.

## Delta Commit Messages
Use `COMMENT` in Delta operations to describe what each write does. This enables an audit trail and makes time-travel debugging meaningful. Example:
```python
df.write.format("delta").option("userMetadata", "silver-load-2024-01-15").save(path)
```
